From b6f8a8a0e16a6bd21c47c39b7c73e0068ef0c27f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:28:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/60] ppc32: restore the 32-bit halves of the ppc backend
 that 13.6 removed

Between 12.4 and 13.6 upstream deleted every 32-bit conditional from the
ppc backend: the file guards became V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 only, 103
`#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 ... #else ... #endif` blocks lost their #else
(the 32-bit instruction choices: lwz/stw for ld/std, lis/ori address
sequences, the two-word double moves, CmpS32 forms, ...), the
`#if !V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64` blocks disappeared outright (the pair
opcodes' code generation, ShiftLeftPair/ShiftRightPair/ShiftRightAlgPair,
the dst_hi/src_hi halves of ConvertDoubleToInt64/MovInt64ToDouble/
MovDoubleToInt64, Is32BitLoadIntoR12), and the 64-bit-only code that
used to sit under a guard (ld/std/divd/mffpr*/rld* wrappers, the
Word64/Int64 opcode cases, DoubleToUint64, MovInt64ComponentsToDouble)
became unconditional.

At the same time the backend's POWER baseline moved to POWER8: the
CpuFeatures::IsSupported(PPC_7_PLUS)/(PPC_8_PLUS) checks went from 6/13 to
0/1 and their fallbacks were dropped - the FP<->GPR moves now use mtfprd/
mffprd/mtfprwa/mtfprwz/mffprwz unconditionally, MinF64/MaxF64 use
xsmindp/xsmaxdp, AssembleArchBoolean uses isel.  None of these exist on a
G4/G5.

This commit puts the 12.4 shape back into the 13.6 files, keeping 13.6's
64-bit code verbatim under V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 and supplying the 12.4
32-bit / pre-POWER7 code otherwise:

- node/reinsert32.py re-inserted the 73 blocks whose 64-bit side still
  exists verbatim in 13.6 (assembler-ppc.h 10, assembler-ppc.cc 14,
  assembler-ppc-inl.h 2, macro-assembler-ppc.h 8, macro-assembler-ppc.cc
  5, code-generator-ppc.cc 30, builtins-ppc.cc 3, simulator-ppc.h 1) and
  restored the nine dual file guards;
- hand-ported where 13.6 rewrote the 64-bit side: set_target_address_at
  (the WritableJitAllocation form of the two-instruction patch),
  ConvertDoubleToInt64 / TryInlineTruncateDoubleToI / TestIfInt32 (hi/lo
  word forms), CallRuntime (RuntimeCEntry(1) on 32-bit), the twelve FP
  move helpers and LoadDoubleLiteral (stack round-trip through
  kExponentOffset/kMantissaOffset), MinF64/MaxF64 (compare-and-branch),
  AssembleArchBoolean (branch around the materialisation), the
  wasm call-target constants (ToInt32), DoubleToInt64/DoubleToUint64 in
  the code generator (64-bit-only VXCVI/isel handling, DoubleToUint64
  64-bit-only), ShiftLeftPair & co (declarations and definitions).
- not touched: the instruction selector (13.6's is Turboshaft-only, with
  no 32-bit block left to re-insert - next commit), the isel uses inside
  the Float32/Double->Int32 conversions and the SIMD helpers (the 12.4
  series patches on those conversions follow in this series; the SIMD
  helpers are never reached, SupportsWasmSimd128() is false below
  POWER9), the disassembler (ENABLE_DISASSEMBLER is off in the harness).

The pair opcodes (kPPC_AddPair ... kPPC_ShiftRightAlgPair) are still in
instruction-codes-ppc.h and the scheduler at 13.6; only their selection
and generation had gone.
